<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 80,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 80,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian barley and 20,000 of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000		 Western white	     7,000</p>
<p>		(April shipment)   Dark northern spring   40,000</p>
<p>					 Hard red winter</p>
<p>					  (13 percent protein)  33,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> Canada     20,000		 Feed (March shipment)  20,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000		 Feed (April shipment)  20,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities desk (81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
